<title>UK: UK M4 up provisional s/a 11.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>UK M4 up provisional s/a 11.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said on Thursday M4 money supply rose a seasonally adjusted 1.3 percent in May for year on year growth of 11.1 percent.  </p>
<p>    MONEY SUPPLY (%)		May		April</p>
<p>    M4 in month   (adjusted)    1.3		 0.2</p>
<p>	 in year to date	    11.1	     10.2</p>
<p>    M4 in month (unadjusted)    1.9		-0.8    in year</p>
<p>to date 11.0 10.0  </p>
<p>Adjusted lending by banks,</p>
<p>    b/societies in blns of stg	9.2     4.4</p>
<p>NOTE - consensus forecast was for 0.7 percent M4 growth on the month for year-on-year growth of 10.0 percent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom + 44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
